  "the_findings": [
    "TIME TO WORK IT IS THE STRONGEST PREDICTOR. L5 pairs 93.3% of 15-minute windows and 65.7% of 5-minute ones, and within a window the rate falls from 82.9% when he opens with 80-100% of it left to 38.0% when he opens with under 20% left.",
    "IMBALANCE IS THE SECOND. A first leg in a balanced book (0.35-0.65) pairs 74.6% of the time on 5-minute windows and 97.7% on 15-minute ones; a lopsided one (<0.20 or >0.80) pairs 49.7% and 33.3%. There is nothing on the far side to pair against.",
    "WORKING THE POSITION SURVIVES ITS CONFOUNDERS. One opening-side price completes 36.8% of the time and four or more completes 93.5%, and that gap does not collapse when window length and time remaining are held fixed -- inside the largest stratum it still runs 43.0% to 93.3%. It is evidence, not proof: a market active enough to reprice into completes for reasons of its own."
  ],
  "transfer_limit": "This history is entirely BTC and ETH up/down windows of 5 and 15 minutes. Our lane trades sports. Time-to-work and far-side liquidity are not crypto-specific mechanisms, but every magnitude here is measured on crypto and none of it is a sports measurement.",
  "no_causal_claim": "These are conditional rates with two confounders held fixed, not an experiment. They say where completion happens, not what would happen if we changed our behaviour."
}